---
import Base from '../layouts/Base.astro';
import {published,stages} from '../lib/content';
const outputs=['Responsibility map & owner dependencies','Relationship factsheet & flows of money','Shortlist, demand evidence & local questions','Unit costs, support costs & cash runway','Capability, accessible funding & territory principles','Responsibilities, timing & evidence','A usable brief, including reasons to pause'];
const selection=['/us-expansion/franchising-vs-licensing/','/states/texas/','/industries/commercial-cleaning/','/cases/cleaning-manager-royalty/'].map(path=>published.find(g=>g.path===path)).filter(Boolean);
---
<Base><section class="container hero"><div class="hero-copy"><span class="eyebrow">FROM AN ESTABLISHED BUSINESS. TO A NEW MARKET.</span><h1>Build a U.S. expansion plan your management team can <em>execute.</em></h1><p class="lede">For owners of established European and Southeast Asian businesses considering franchising or licensing. Work through the rules, economics, and partner decisions—one step at a time.</p><div class="hero-footer"><span>Built for management-run businesses</span><span>B2B services & consumer businesses</span></div></div><aside class="hero-aside" aria-label="What your expansion brief will contain"><div class="sheet-top"><span>YOUR U.S. EXPANSION BRIEF</span><span>WORKING DOCUMENT / 01</span></div><div class="sheet-title">A plan the whole team can work from.</div><div class="brief-flow"><div class="flow-row"><span class="flow-no">01</span><div><strong>What we know</strong><p>Our operating model, customer evidence and responsibilities.</p></div></div><div class="flow-row"><span class="flow-no">02</span><div><strong>What we need to test</strong><p>Economics, local requirements and partner capability.</p></div></div><div class="flow-row"><span class="flow-no">03</span><div><strong>Who does what next</strong><p>Named owners, dependencies and unresolved decisions.</p></div></div></div><div class="sheet-foot">YOUR DECISIONS + YOUR ASSUMPTIONS + TRACEABLE SOURCES</div></aside></section><div class="container" style="padding-top:0;padding-bottom:0"><div class="context-strip"><div><span>01 /</span>Understand the relevant rule.</div><div><span>02 /</span>See it in a realistic business.</div><div><span>03 /</span>Prepare one useful next step.</div></div></div><section class="container"><div class="section-heading"><div><span class="eyebrow">THE PATH FROM IDEA TO DECISION</span><h2>Seven stages.<br/>One considered brief.</h2></div><p>Move at your own pace. Explore later stages. Keep gaps visible rather than turning them into green ticks.</p></div><div class="journey-list">{stages.map((s,i)=><div class="journey-row"><span class="number">0{i+1}</span><h3>{s}</h3><p>{outputs[i]}</p></div>)}</div></section><section class="dark-band"><div class="container"><div><span class="eyebrow">A SMALL CHANGE. A DIFFERENT DECISION.</span><h2>A profitable business<br/>isn’t yet a transferable model.</h2><p>In this fictional Singapore cleaning business, a dedicated manager and a revenue royalty consume the apparent operating surplus. The useful question is what would need to change.</p><a class="text-link" href="/tools/us-unit-economics/">Inspect the model and its assumptions <span class="arrow-icon" aria-hidden="true"></span></a></div><div class="worked-math"><p class="micro-note">ILLUSTRATIVE ONLY · USD / YEAR · $1M REVENUE</p><div class="math-line"><span>Surplus before manager & royalty</span><strong>$180,000</strong></div><div class="math-line"><span>Fully loaded general manager</span><strong>− $120,000</strong></div><div class="math-line"><span>6% revenue royalty</span><strong>− $60,000</strong></div><div class="math-line math-total"><span>Surplus at this stage</span><strong>$0</strong></div><p class="micro-note" style="margin-top:18px">Before any other omitted obligations. Operating profit and available cash are different measures.</p></div></div></section><section class="container"><div class="section-heading"><div><span class="eyebrow">THE REFERENCE DESK</span><h2>Read first.<br/>Apply when you’re ready.</h2></div><p>Complete public answers, source links and practical preparation. No email address required.</p></div><div class="library-list">{selection.map(g=><a class="library-row" href={g.path}><span class="category">{g.family?.replaceAll('-',' ')}</span><div><h3>{g.title}</h3><p>{g.description}</p></div><span class="arrow" aria-hidden="true"><span class="arrow-icon" aria-hidden="true"></span></span></a>)}</div><p class="meta" style="margin-top:24px"><a href="/guides/">Browse the field guides</a> · <a href="/coverage/">See researched coverage and remaining gaps</a></p></section><section class="container section-border grid-two"><div><span class="eyebrow">EVIDENCE BEFORE CONFIDENCE</span><h2>A licence label<br/>doesn’t settle the rule.</h2></div><div><p>What will the partner receive? Who pays whom? What support and operating controls are involved? Which jurisdictions are connected to the offer?</p><p class="muted">Those facts matter more than the agreement’s title. Our tools help your team prepare the facts and identify questions requiring judgment. They don’t issue legal clearance.</p><a class="text-link" href="/methodology/">How we research and review sources <span class="arrow-icon" aria-hidden="true"></span></a></div></section></Base>
